# Git Branching

This rule is the local branching standard for the shared `.cursor` system and aligned product work.

Authoritative schedule and roles: `docs/AUTONOMOUS-GIT-OPERATIONS.md` and `docs/adr/0003-autonomous-ship-pull-promote.md`.

## Integration branch

- **`development`** is the integration branch for factory merges by the delivery controller.

## Branch prefixes

| Prefix | Use | Merge target |
|--------|-----|--------------|
| `issue/<id>-<slug>` | **Studio default** — one short-lived branch per governed issue | **`development`** (delivery controller only) |
| `dev/<machine><ide>` | Rare ad-hoc IDE work only (not forever home) | **`development`** via PR |
| `cursor/*` | Cloud / dashboard agent work | **`development`** via PR |
| Promotion | `development` → `staging` → `main` | See promotion flow below |

Bootstrap new sessions with `/agentsetup`. Migrate already-open dirty/wrong-branch sessions with `/agentcomply`.

## Promotion flow

```
issue/* or dev/* or cursor/*  →  Phase PR to development
  →  Bugbot / Review Gate  →  delivery controller merges when named gates + receipt pass
development  →  staging   (Tue & Fri 10:00 Asia/Taipei, auto via delivery controller)
staging      →  main      (Mon 08:00 package; Principal Approve ~08:30 via Lisa/Telegram)
```

- **Delivery controller** merges only into **`development`** through GitHub protection.
- **Delivery controller** promotes **`development` → `staging`** on schedule when receipt identity holds.
- **Principal** approves **`staging` → `main`** (Lisa Telegram). Not a code review of every PR.
- Module 6 **product Release OK / live deploy** remains a separate Principal gate.
- Allowed PR sources into `development` are enforced in `.github/workflows/branch-source-policy.yml`.

## Commit messages

Conventional commits: `type(scope): summary`.
